# text = But for all that and granting to the full the offensiveness , the folly , the unchristianness of Mr . Hamper's way of speaking to you in recommending his friend's book , yet if it told you what he said it did , that wages find their own level , and that the most successful strike can only force them up for a moment , to sink in far greater proportion afterwards , in consequence of that very strike , the book would have told you the truth Well , sir I wish some of the kindest and wisest of the masters would meet some of you men , and have a good talk on these things ; it would , surely , be the best way of getting over your difficulties , which , I do believe , arise from your ignorance -- excuse me , Mr . Higgins -- on subjects which it is for the mutual interest of both masters and men should be well understood by both .
