# text = But the truth is , these country clergymen live such isolated lives -- isolated , I mean , from all intercourse with men of equal cultivation with themselves , by whose minds they might regulate their own , and discover when they were going either too fast or too slow -- that they are very apt to disturb themselves with imaginary doubts as to the articles of faith , and throw up certain opportunities of doing good for very uncertain fancies of their own I differ from you .
