# text = Other people prosper and grow rich , and hold their paltry names high and dry above shame Shame never touched me I sometimes have wondered where justice was gone to , and now I don't believe there is such a thing in the world ,-- now you are come to this ; you , my own John Thornton , though you and I may be beggars together -- my own dear son Mother who has sent me my lot in life , both of good and of evil Mother I , too , have been rebellious ; but I am striving to be so no longer .
